From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 09:30:00 +0200
Subject: drm/msm/dp: handle the HPD replug interrupt

Commit 5043357e75ba ("drm/msm/dp: rework HPD handling") stopped reading
DP_DP_HPD_REPLUG_INT_MASK. The bit is still unmasked and the hardware
still raises it, so a sink that drops HPD and reasserts it while the
controller stays enabled goes unnoticed: its capabilities and its EDID
are never reread and the connector keeps describing the display that was
there before.

Drive a full disconnect and reconnect from the interrupt, because a bare
connected notification is swallowed as a repeat of the state the
connector already holds. Leave the audio jack alone here: the modeset
that follows runs the enable path, which signals the connect event once
video is up.

Fixes: 5043357e75ba ("drm/msm/dp: rework HPD handling")
Signed-off-by: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c | 14 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -955,6 +955,20 @@ static irqreturn_t msm_dp_display_irq_thread(int irq, void *dev_id)
 		drm_bridge_hpd_notify(dp->msm_dp_display.bridge,
 				      connector_status_connected);
 
+	/*
+	 * A replug means the sink went away and came back while the controller
+	 * was left enabled, so its capabilities and its EDID may both differ
+	 * now. Drive a full disconnect and reconnect to reread them; a bare
+	 * connected notification would be swallowed as a repeat of the state
+	 * the connector is already in.
+	 */
+	if (hpd_isr_status & DP_DP_HPD_REPLUG_INT_MASK) {
+		drm_bridge_hpd_notify(dp->msm_dp_display.bridge,
+				      connector_status_disconnected);
+		drm_bridge_hpd_notify(dp->msm_dp_display.bridge,
+				      connector_status_connected);
+	}
+
 	if (hpd_isr_status & DP_DP_IRQ_HPD_INT_MASK) {
 		rc = pm_runtime_resume_and_get(&pdev->dev);
 		if (rc)
